   "Cross out radicular cyst: this also arises from a necrotic pulp, so a vital tooth essentially rules it out.",
   "Cross out cemento-osseous dysplasia: the tooth is vital, but it most commonly involves multiple lower anterior teeth and the lamina dura is lost at the affected apices.",
